      "progress": "The compact translation hull carries an invariant Borel probability measure, constructed from actual continuous Euclidean box averages. Coordinate-box volumes and positive normalized averaging functionals are proved. Symmetric differences lie in fixed-thickness shells whose relative volumes tend to zero; change of variables and an integral bound give vanishing translation error. Banach-Alaoglu and Riesz-Markov-Kakutani then give the invariant probability measure, both for general continuous Euclidean actions and specifically for the paper hull. The Koopman operators are constructed with the manuscript convention U_z f(Γ)=f(Γ+z), hence pullback by T_{-z}. They are unitaries, obey the additive group law, and form a strongly continuous representation on the separable stationary L² space. Constants are invariant and the constant one has norm one. Finite injective point matching controls compactly supported test integrals. Weak convergence therefore implies vague convergence. A compactly supported bump distinguishes different configurations, so the continuous counting-test map is injective; compactness makes it an embedding and proves the converse. All mathematical components of this node compile and pass all 15 integrated linters. The standalone compiles and the complete 245-declaration transitive axiom audit uses only standard Lean axioms."
